  "sourceFindings": [
    "Locked prisma/client/engines/fetch-engine versions are 6.19.3 and engines-version pins c2990dca591cba766e3b7ef5d9e8a84796e47ab7.",
    "The failed original workspace contains both official-hash @prisma/engines native artifacts, but both node_modules/prisma generator targets are absent. Integration helper dependency state is distinct and is not evidence of original-workspace readiness.",
    "CLI ensureNeededBinariesExist targets node_modules/@prisma/engines; bundled generate getBinaryPathsByVersion gle targets node_modules/prisma for this same-version generator.",
    "All six bound code-source hashes and seven excerpt hashes match. Excerpt bodies after removing appended presentation LF match their declared raw UTF8 byte offsets; they are not verbatim full-file byte slices including that appended LF.",
    "Cache-hit eligibility requires the logical cache binary plus an exact lowercase 64-byte checksum sidecar without filename, whitespace or newline. Raw official checksum response text cannot be used directly as the cache sidecar.",
    "An existing invalid cache can force download even with an existing valid target. Target-only native-version fallback invokes native code and is not a statically established readiness guarantee.",
    "The downloader validates compressed and decompressed published hashes when downloading archives. Existing raw binaries are independently equal to the corresponding official uncompressed hashes; gzip checksum files alone do not prove a downloaded gzip artifact.",
    "Linux default cache is os.homedir()/.cache/prisma/master/<engineVersion>/<platform>; R12 sanitizer strips XDG_CACHE_HOME. A fixed alternate cache setting requires separately reviewed R13 authority and exact environment binding."
  ],
  "futureProvisioningPreconditions": [
